<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Syria</h1><p class="st-meta">1925 CE – 1930 CE · capital Damascus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The unified Syrian state created by France in 1925 from Damascus and Aleppo, the setting of the Great Syrian Revolt.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> merged the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-damascus">State of Damascus</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-aleppo">State of Aleppo</a> into the State of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> with effect from 1 January 1925, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> as capital and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subhi-barakat">Subhi Barakat</a> as president; the Alawite and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabal-al-druze">Jabal Druze</a> states remained separate.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Months after its creation, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-syrian-revolt">Great Syrian Revolt</a> spread from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabal-al-druze">Jabal Druze</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and the countryside; French forces shelled Damascus in October 1925 and suppressed the rising by 1927. French high commissioners appointed governments led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-nami">Ahmad Nami</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taj-al-din-al-hasani">Taj al-Din al-Hasani</a>. A Constituent Assembly elected in 1928, dominated by the nationalist National Bloc under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hashim-al-atassi">Hashim al-Atassi</a>, drafted a constitution.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In May 1930 the French high commissioner promulgated a modified constitution, turning the state into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-republic">Syrian Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-syria.jpg" alt="State of Syria" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: F l a n k e r · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Syria_French_mandate.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1925 CE – 1930 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Damascus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Subhi Barakat, Ahmad Nami, Taj al-Din al-Hasani</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Syrian State</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1928&amp;focus=state-of-syria" aria-label="State of Syria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5607 962 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Syria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5927 1218L5927 1218M5927 1218L5936 1127M5927 1218L5936 1127M5927 1218L5905 1205M5927 1218L5927 1218"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5927 1218h0M5936 1127h0M5936 1127h0M5905 1205h0M5927 1218h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5927 1218h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5927 1218h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Damascus. <a href="/atlas?year=1928&amp;focus=state-of-syria">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
